# UEFI firmware layer: intentions for machines that boot via UEFI.
#
# Intentions ONLY. The package manager owns dependency closure; never
# enumerate resolved dependencies here (saphira-profiles(5)).
#
# saphira-image appends this layer to every uefi-* target (and to
# nothing else), so a UEFI installation carries its ESP and NVRAM
# tooling while a BIOS installation never sees EFI-specific utilities.
# Installer environments are exempt by design: the firmware a USB
# stick boots from is not necessarily the firmware of the image it
# writes, so installer profiles (saphira-installer, usb-installer)
# keep both toolchains explicitly instead of through this layer.
#
# Removable fallback versus NVRAM entries, deliberately distinguished:
# a removable EFI binary (BOOTX64.EFI) boots with no NVRAM state at
# all, so a machine that boots only that way never invokes efibootmgr
# and it sits inert. NVRAM boot-entry management - what a kernel
# upgrade that re-points the boot entry needs - is the reason
# efibootmgr is here rather than only in installer payloads.
efibootmgr
dosfstools
